OL,3,GNEWSACamden Council at 'sharp end of
OL,4,Athe housing crisis'
OL,5,
OL,6,FHundreds of affordable homes originally
OL,7,Fpromised for major Camden developments
OL,8,Fhave been lost or are at risk after
OL,9,Fdevelopers sought reductions to housing
OL,10,Fquotas, citing worsening economic
OL,11,Fconditions.
OL,13,FIn an eight-acre development named
OL,14,FCamden Goods Yard, a revised plan
OL,15,Fsuccessful on appeal saw affordable
OL,16,Fhomes slashed from 203 to 83 in May.
OL,18,FOn Thursday the council approved
OL,19,Frevised plans to cut affordable housing
OL,20,Fat the O2 Centre site from 570 homes to
OL,21,F330 on their 1,800-home development.
OL,23,APub: 24-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
